                "end": 4,
                "start": 4
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to North Carolina Department of Revenue, the petitioner argues that a state\u2019s pro\u2011rata tax on trust income complies with due process because trust beneficiaries are the true owners of the income."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Petitioner Position \u2013 North Carolina Department of Revenue",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. O'Neil",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "b95094278ea0a0ae23a34ee9a37691e5536b8fbd83f48470928be4f96efb3056",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-b95094278ea0-0002-0006"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 46,
                "start": 46
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. O'Neil, the respondent maintains that a state may tax a beneficiary when the beneficiary has an absolute right to the income in a particular year."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. O'Neil",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "b95094278ea0a0ae23a34ee9a37691e5536b8fbd83f48470928be4f96efb3056",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-b95094278ea0-0002-0008"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 56,
                "start": 56
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. O'Neil, if the beneficiary had a vested right in a certain percentage of the trust, then we would treat her as having a current interest in that trust."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. O'Neil",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "b95094278ea0a0ae23a34ee9a37691e5536b8fbd83f48470928be4f96efb3056",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-b95094278ea0-0002-0011"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 54,
                "start": 54
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. O'Neil, a state could enact a wealth tax if the person being taxed has a current vested right to the assets and the right is alienable."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Respondent Position \u2013 The Kimberley Rice Kaestner 1992 Family Trust",
